From: overpressure <overpressure@pico4>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: a refresh change is a mode set on DPU 6.0

Valve's seamless path for a refresh-only change, written for the Frame's DPU 10.0, leaves the XR2's
DPU 6.0 at the old rate: the state says 72 Hz, vblanks stay 11.11 ms apart and the compositor
judders. Without it the change is an ordinary mode set: the panels power-cycle on the new timing.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c
@@ -486,6 +486,11 @@
 static bool dpu_kms_seamless_timing_update(struct msm_kms *kms,
 					   struct drm_display_mode *mode)
 {
+	/*
+	 * The seamless path does not change the timing here: a full mode set instead.
+	 */
+	if (to_dpu_kms(kms)->catalog->mdss_ver->core_major_ver < 10)
+		return false;
 	mode = dpu_encoder_find_connector_mode(mode);
 	if (!mode)
 		return false;
